{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1117198-standard-fantasy-campaign-using-mage","id":1117198,"title":"Standard Fantasy Campaign using Mage?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-17T08:09:00-07:00","id":1117198,"title":"Standard Fantasy Campaign using Mage?","content":"So two things I've been considering. One is mage in a fantasy setting a la dungeons and dragons.<br /> <br /> And second is completely wiping the spheres in favor of Player specific spheres.<br /> <br /> Basically, the idea is that I meet up with each player and talk about the character they want to make. Come up with spheres that work for that concept. And move on. For example a sphere of theivery. At rank 1 you can detect opportunity for thefts. At rank 2 you can hide these opportunities or give yourself bonuses to steal something. At rank 3 you could set a thieves lure or curse. Basically +/- successes to all rolls while trying to steal the item you place the spell on. At rank 4 you could create opportunity for theft where none before. And at rank 5 you could create opportunity for theft where it doesn't make sense. Like stealing the flame off a candle or some such similar feat.<br /> <br /> But essentially the idea is to go through and build the world partially out of the ideas they come up with for spheres. So each has a vested interest and connection to the world. If Joe wants to be Joe the chthulhu summoner. It means he wants chthulhus in the world.<br /> <br /> The one concern I have is the potential lack of balance between sphere concepts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T08:24:56-07:00","id":1117206,"title":"","content":"First I recommend dark eras, it's good for inspiration.<br /> <br /> Second, unless you're just doing &quot;MAGE IN FANTASY LAND&quot; it might be easier to use hunter the vigil. Has less powers but it's more flexible especially the upcoming 2e which has 'build your own endowment' rules good for everything from paladins and alchemists to warlocks (in terms of D&amp;D-esque classes). Might even be worth trotting out witchfinders and letting them use those magic rules (which suits your custom sphere idea). Other options are second sight and the influence based mages somewhere in these forums.<br /> <br /> Mage's problem is that it tends to dominate and consume games it's in, and here that would translate to mage dominating every other character aspect. No warriors who aren't adamantine arrow (or equivalent for your setting), no clerics who aren't obrimos, druids are just thysus, ect. custom spheres would be difficult to balance as basically your first half dozen sessions would be nothing but creative thaumaturgy and the players could (through no fault of their own) break the game by trying to find ways to use their custom powers for every situation.<br /> <br /> This doubles as the nature of a fantasy setting means everyone knows magic is real so it's likely that while paradox may exist it's unlikely that anyone would be considered a sleeper. So basically you'd be in a world about duels between sorcerer kings warring for power across a mystical land. Which can be awesome if that's what you want to play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","name":"Darkfoxdev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T08:37:03-07:00","id":1117211,"title":"","content":"I was basically going to handwave paradox as the wrath of D&amp;D style active gods. Punishing vain mages for their hubris.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T10:44:03-07:00","id":1117277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically, the idea is that I meet up with each player and talk about the character they want to make. Come up with spheres that work for that concept. And move on. For example a sphere of theivery. At rank 1 you can detect opportunity for thefts. At rank 2 you can hide these opportunities or give yourself bonuses to steal something. At rank 3 you could set a thieves lure or curse. Basically +/- successes to all rolls while trying to steal the item you place the spell on. At rank 4 you could create opportunity for theft where none before. And at rank 5 you could create opportunity for theft where it doesn't make sense. Like stealing the flame off a candle or some such similar feat.</div> </div> </div> </div>You may want to take a look to DA:Mage system, as it's something akin (Batini have a Sphere of Secrets that works very well with thiefs, and there are several &quot;warrior spheres&quot;).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The one concern I have is the potential lack of balance between sphere concepts. </div> </div> </div>This is, indeed, hard. To the point that, arguably, Spheres themselves aren't truly balanced. DA may provide insight, albeit Pillars aren't well balanced.In the end, common sense and experience shall guide you through the perilous journey, and the end product is, likely, going to be somewhat unbalanced.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So two things I've been considering. One is mage in a fantasy setting a la dungeons and dragons.<br /> .<br /> .<br /> .<br /> I was basically going to handwave paradox as the wrath of D&amp;D style active gods. Punishing vain mages for their hubris. </div> </div> </div>Perhaps you may want to look at Cruzade, as there Paradox it's akin to God's wrath.<br /> <br /> If you do not allow for impresive feats, Magick ain't going to be that EPIC, in D&amp;D gods do not punish every little fireball. Paradox shouldn't be that punitive in such a world, only attacking really outrageous feats<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkfoxdev</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mage's problem is that it tends to dominate and consume games it's in</div> </div> </div> </div>And spellcasters do not dominate D&amp;D in the long run? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> In all truth, if you do not want the supernatural power of mages to overshadow the epic knight, give them epic static powers that allow them to stand in the face of evil magick (it's not like powerful D&amp;D warriors are as fragile as normal humans). Same with everyone","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 07-17-2017, 01:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T10:53:01-07:00","id":1117280,"title":"","content":"Er... If you want to run fantasy games, there are plenty of games proposing settings and rules... If you throw the WoD (mostly taking place in an urban environment) and the Sphere System, what are you keeping of the original game ? Hence my question, in what way will it be a Mage game ? It is just to understand the question and think about appropriate ideas <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Do you have ideas of plots for your campaign ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T11:52:37-07:00","id":1117342,"title":"","content":"I'm not throwing out the sphere system. Just the default spheres.<br /> <br /> And yes Aleph, I'd mostly be retaining paradox as a ready made excuse to stop the people I soundboard my crazy ideas with from emulating me.<br /> <br /> As to why? My group is pretty D&amp;D centric. They've turned down several different games but I think more than anything else it's the setting of D&amp;D that they like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T11:53:13-07:00","id":1117344,"title":"","content":"I once ran a SpellJammer D&amp;D campaign using WoD rules. I had magic following Sorcerer path rules. The Sorcerers were the movers and shakers of all things magic. Mages were known in legends as being powerful and crazy. I treated all difficulties for casting as Vulgar without witnesses. Paradox was calculated according to subtlety. Coincidental magic was performed by following Hedge Path rules for casting times and rituals; or making it look like magic wasn't used at all. Showy magic that skipped from the paradigm was treated as Vulgar without witnesses. All paradox points only applied to Quiet though; hence the crazy. The one Mage player learned to keep things subtle real fast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3138-old-rusty-pipe","name":"Old Rusty Pipe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T13:55:31-07:00","id":1117425,"title":"","content":"GURPS Thaumatology has spheres as realm-based magic. That would be worth looking at for a fantasy mage game.<br /> <br /> As for D&amp;D, which D&amp;D setting are you talking about? D&amp;D has had many published settings and many settings created by individual groups.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T15:09:54-07:00","id":1117464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>baakyocalder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1117198-standard-fantasy-campaign-using-mage?p=1117425#post1117425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">GURPS Thaumatology has spheres as realm-based magic. That would be worth looking at for a fantasy mage game.<br /> <br /> As for D&amp;D, which D&amp;D setting are you talking about? D&amp;D has had many published settings and many settings created by individual groups.</div> </div> </div> </div>In general we make our own settings, but they all have a fairly similar D&amp;D feel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T12:14:54-07:00","id":1118656,"title":"","content":"If the goal is to keep them in the DnD-style setting, why not just import the rules as they are, and tell them that in this world Mages fulfill many roles? I mean, the existing Spheres can let people do most anything they can imagine. A thief would pick up Correspondence and maybe Forces or Life, etc.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}